* Course 07 final exam -- the AC answers (Questions 6, 9, 10, 11, 12, 13 and 14) confirmed in ngspice.
* Each block is a separate circuit; every circuit is solved at each analysis frequency, and each block's
* results are read after the analysis at its own frequency. In ngspice i(V) is the current entering the
* source's + node, so the current a source delivers is -i(V). Phases are converted to degrees.
* Q6: 10 V peak at 1e4 rad/s; (6t) R2 removed for the Thevenin voltage; (6z) source zeroed and a 1 A
*     test current for Z_Th; (6m) the conjugate-matched load 19.2308 ohm + 615.38 uH.
* Q10: K couples the coils (k = 0.9, dots at each inductor's first node); a second pair in series aiding.
* Q11: the resistive T network driven (a) into a 50 ohm load, (b) by 2 V behind 50 ohm (S11 = V1 - 1,
*      S21 = V2), (c) from port 2 the same way (S22).
* Q12: RMS phasors; balanced delta load 30 + j40 ohm (40 ohm = 127.324 mH at 50 Hz); a second copy has
*      the 152.789 uF star-connected capacitors added.
* Q13: the 5.4019 V fundamental applied at the switch node, with and without the 10 mohm ESR.
* Q14: the L-section (1.43575 nH, 2.29720 pF) into 12.5 ohm, driven by 1 V for Z_in.
*
* EXPECT q6e   key:solutions.md#X07.6e rtol=2e-4
* EXPECT q6f   key:solutions.md#X07.6f rtol=2e-4
* EXPECT q6g   key:solutions.md#X07.6g rtol=2e-4
* EXPECT q6h   key:solutions.md#X07.6h rtol=2e-4
